# Line-ending policy lives here, not in each contributor's core.autocrlf.
# `text=auto` canonicalizes every file git detects as text to LF *in the
# repository*; working trees may still use CRLF on Windows if that's the
# local preference.
* text=auto

# Binary fixtures. These are byte-compared by the round-trip tests, so make
# their exemption explicit rather than relying on git's NUL-byte heuristic.
# (`binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff`.)
*.dbn  binary
*.dbz  binary
*.zst  binary
*.frag binary
